CR-03 follow-up: the craft edit-intent detector is verb-gated, so ordinary questions no
longer auto-open the Craft editor; all gates green (commit 4cb92f2).

## The defect this fixes
The post-commit audit found a real bug in my own `CRAFT_EDIT_INTENT_RE`: the alternation
listed bare nouns alongside edit verbs (`document`, `layout`, `paragraph`, `size`,
`color`, `background`, `page`, ...). Because those nouns are exactly the words an
innocent question uses, **13 of 20 innocent questions matched** and auto-opened the
editor: "what is this document about?", "is this document editable?", "how many pages are
in this document?", "what color is the background?". Confirmed with a throwaway vitest
probe before changing anything, so the defect was measured rather than assumed.

## Root cause, and the second bug it hid
The regex was noun-based instead of verb-based, so a mention of a file was treated as a
request to edit it. Fixing that exposed a second, independent bug: **JS `\b` only treats
`[A-Za-z0-9_]` as word characters**, so `\b` never matches around an Arabic letter and the
Arabic verb list matched nothing at all. Both had to be fixed together.

## What changed in `autoOpen.ts`
- Arabic elements now use Unicode property lookarounds (`(?<![\p{L}\p{N}])` /
  `(?!\p{L}\p{N})`) instead of `\b`, and the RegExp is compiled with the `u` flag, which
  `\p{...}` requires. The English elements keep `\b`, since their operands are ASCII.
- Every entry is now a verb or verb phrase: `edit|modify|reformat|restyle|retouch|
  redesign|reframe|fix|update|change|revise|polish|tweak|add|insert|append|remove|delete|
  replace|rearrange|reorder|resort|crop|cut|trim|resize|rescale|rotate|flip|scale|zoom|
  enhance|brighten|darken|sharpen|blur|recolor|recolour|realign|align|indent|merge|split|
  export|print|save as|download as` (Arabic equivalents in the same shape).
- Bare nouns are gone. `color`/`colour` alone is not intent (only `recolor`); `download`
  alone is not intent (only `download as`), so "can you download this for me?" no longer
  matches.
- Soft-request openers (`please`, `can you`, `could you`, `would you`, `i want`,
  `i need`, `lets` / Arabic `أريد`, `أحتاج`, `لو سمحت`, `من فضلك`) only count when an
  edit verb follows in the same span, so "I want to download a file" stays inert.
- "make the background darker" is handled explicitly (`make` + a comparative within two
  words), because the comparative is the request and `darker` alone is ambiguous.
- The malformed array left by the earlier patch (an element closed early, orphaning the
  following `+ '...'` continuations) is repaired; the module now parses.

## Tests
`workspace/__tests__/craftAutoOpen.test.ts` gained two cases that pin the new behaviour:
- "does not match innocent questions that only mention a file" — 21 questions that must
  NOT match, including the 13 that previously matched.
- "still matches real edit requests" — 10 requests that MUST match.
The existing Arabic cases (`صمّم الغلاف وأضف بطاقة`, `أضف تأثير الأزرق عليها`,
`عدّل الفقرة الأولى`) and the pre-existing `autoOpen.test.ts` case ("Please cut the
document", which needs `cut`) all still pass. No test was weakened or skipped; the only
edit to an existing file added coverage.

## Gates (run from the worktree root on the committed tree, 4cb92f2)
- `npx tsc --noEmit` (root)                        -> exit 0
- `(cd packages/web && npx tsc --noEmit)`          -> exit 0
- `npm run build:server`                           -> exit 0 (dist/server.cjs 19.3mb)
- `(cd packages/web && npx next build)`           -> exit 0 (compiled successfully)
- `(cd packages/web && npx vitest run)`           -> 75 files / 504 tests, all pass
- `npm run check:encoding`                         -> OK (no BOM, no mojibake, all JSON valid)

The throwaway probe and the one-shot repair scripts were deleted before committing; the
working tree is clean and both commits are on `khamis1992/cr-03`.

