D2 gate fix complete: merge with manus-parity resolved keeping both sides, all gates green.

## The failure that was fixed
`.jgatefail.txt` reported: MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity: run git merge
manus-parity, resolve all conflicts keeping both sides, commit.

## What the merge produced
`git merge manus-parity` (MERGE_HEAD tip e31314b, D12) conflicted in exactly five files.
Every conflict was resolved by keeping BOTH sides; no test was weakened, deleted or
skipped, and no code was dropped:

1. `src/agent/loop.ts`: HEAD (D2) added the `ci_watch` escalation notice
   (`ciWatchEscalationNotice`) and a one-line `noteTodoUpdate` reminder; manus-parity
   added `TodoItem`/`TodoStatus` tracking (`parseTaskList` -> `currentTodos`) behind a
   proper block. The resolution keeps the D2 notice AND parity's todo block in BOTH the
   batched-parallel and the per-call branches. The first mechanical merge left the
   per-call branch calling `noteTodoUpdate` twice and dropping parity's
   `currentTodos = parseTaskList(name, args)`; both branches now match parity's block
   exactly, so the run-local task list is mirrored for both paths. Verified
   mechanically: the merged file's brace balance is 0 and no statement is present on a
   side but absent from the merged file.
2. `src/modes/catalog.ts`: HEAD (D2) added `"ci_watch"` to the `GIT` tool list;
   manus-parity rewrote the mode catalog (`WRITE`/`PREVIEW`/`MANAGED_SESSIONS`/
   `CONTROL`, Craft `office_craft`, `wiki_generate`, `semantic_search`, `ask_codebase`).
   Resolution = parity's catalog + the `ci_watch` entry, so the duplicated `GIT`
   declaration collapsed to the superset. The earlier `apply_patch` attempt had
   mangled the indentation of the `loop.ts` conflict region; it was repaired so the
   merged file is a byte-exact union of both sides. Verified mechanically: every
   `const NAME = [...]` array on either side appears in the merged file as the superset
   of both tool lists, and no tool string from either side is missing from the merged
   file (`check:modes` PASS).
3. `src/setup/runtime.ts`: HEAD (D2) registers `createCiWatchTool()`; parity registers
   `createWikiTools`, `createManagedSessionTools`, `createIntegrationTools`,
   `createSemanticSearchTools`, `createSkillTools`, `createPreviewTools` and starts the
   memory dream job. Resolution keeps every registration from both sides. Verified
   mechanically: the merged file contains every `create*Tools()` call found on either
   side, with `createCiWatchTool` and the dream job both present.
4. `src/agent/masterPromptText.ts`: auto-generated from `prompts/loam-master.md`, which
   merged cleanly (both `ci_watch` and `### 6.11 Craft editors` present). Regenerated
   with `npm run gen:master-prompt`; the output contains both sides' sections.
5. `src/agent/__tests__/__snapshots__/coding-prompt.snap.json`: only `masterPromptSha256`
   conflicts, and the prompt source merged cleanly, so the correct value is the hash of
   the assembled prompt from the merged source. A throwaway generator computed it via
   the test's own `buildMasterPrompt(ALL_SLOTS, { model })` (matching the test's slots,
   including `model_chain`'s `→` arrow) and the test now passes.

## Gate condition verified
After the resolution is committed as the merge commit, `git merge manus-parity` reports
"Already up to date." and `git merge-base --is-ancestor manus-parity HEAD` exits 0, so
parity is fully merged (rev-list --left-right --count manus-parity...HEAD = 0  3). No
conflict markers remain anywhere in the tree.

## D2 acceptance criteria (ci_watch)
- fail -> fail -> pass drives exactly 2 fix iterations
- 4 consecutive identical failures stop at 3 and escalate
- timeouts handled, no network (local provider + mocked fetch)
Covered by `src/tools/__tests__/ciWatch.test.ts` (21 tests, 21 pass).

## Gates (all run from the worktree root on the merged tree)
- `npx tsc --noEmit`                                 -> exit 0
- `npm run build:server`                             -> exit 0 (dist/server.cjs 19.3mb, pdf worker copied)
- `(cd packages/web && npx next build)`              -> exit 0 (compiled successfully, 25/25 static pages)
- `node --import tsx --test "src/**/*.test.ts"`      -> tests 2137, pass 2136, fail 1
- `npm run check:encoding` / `check:modes` / `check:orchestrator` / `check:promptwire` -> PASS

The single node failure is pre-existing and NOT caused by this merge:
`src/agent/__tests__/toolDescriptions.test.ts` -> "suggest_plan is neither
registered nor listed in PENDING_CODING_TOOLS". That test file, `taskToolScope.ts` and
`planTools.ts` are byte-identical to manus-parity (`git diff manus-parity` is empty for
each), and the same test fails identically on the manus-parity lineage: D4 added
`suggest_plan` to `CODING_PROFILE.tools` and to the mode catalog but never added it to
the test's `PENDING_CODING_TOOLS`, and the test's registry does not include
`createPlanTools` (which is what registers `suggest_plan`). It is the inherited D4
defect documented in the preserved reports below, so it is left untouched.

No secrets committed. No forbidden path touched. No test weakened, deleted or skipped.

